cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "anti-slop: structural detection and repair of substance defects in AI-assisted work"
message: "If you use this project or its verification ledger, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Agrici
    given-names: Daniel
repository-code: "https://github.com/AgriciDaniel/anti-slop"
abstract: >
  A structural approach to finding and repairing substance defects in
  AI-assisted prose, code, documentation, and agent output. It reports defects
  and never reports authorship. The design follows from a measurement: LLM
  judges agree with human slop labels at approximately chance, and their errors
  favour the surface features that define slop, so every check is a mechanical
  procedure producing a verifiable artifact rather than a model judgement.
  Ships a source ledger of 43 dated entries with evidence tiers and stated
  limitations, and a verification ledger recording eight corrections to figures
  that circulate incorrectly in this field.
keywords:
  - ai-slop
  - writing-quality
  - code-quality
  - citation-verification
  - research-integrity
  - claude-code
